# Archived gate logs and their manifest are evidence: checkout must not rewrite
# their bytes (core.autocrlf=true on this host would otherwise turn LF into
# CRLF and make logs.sha256 fail against its own files).
evidence/viewmodel/range/logs/** -text
# core.autocrlf=true is on for this checkout, and it would rewrite the evidence
# here on checkout: every line of artifacts.sha256 is `sha256 *<path>`, so a
# trailing CR becomes part of the filename, and the .txt/.json/.csv extracts would
# come back with different bytes than the ones that were hashed. Both failures
# appear in exactly the situation the receipt exists for -- a fresh clone -- so
# this directory is checked out byte for byte.
evidence/weapon-material/** -text
# T30: the inventory TSV, the gate summary and the frozen frames are evidence whose
# bytes the report's sha256 lines describe. core.autocrlf=true on this host would
# otherwise rewrite the text files on checkout and make the report's hashes describe
# a different file. Checked out byte for byte, like evidence/weapon-material/**.
evidence/t30/** -text

# T68: the golden event fixtures and the same-tick table are evidence whose bytes
# the gate hashes (same-tick-334.tsv sha256 9d6817c9...). core.autocrlf=true on
# this host rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, which moved that hash to 18f506ff...
# and made the gate fail against its own fixture. Checked out byte for byte.
evidence/t68-events/** -text

# T85/task-24: the launch-hygiene baseline is a set of script|flag keys compared
# byte-wise by the gate. It is committed LF and read LF so that the file git
# checks out, the file --update-baseline rewrites, and the file the ratchet
# compares all agree on a fresh clone.
evidence/gate-launch-hygiene/baseline.txt text eol=lf

