evidence/t100-userinfo/** -text

# --- line-ending governance (N25; ruled 2026-11-14, applied 2026-11-18) ---
# The sources, the build definitions and every gate script are read as text by
# tools that care about the byte before the newline. A CRLF checkout is not
# cosmetic: bash reports "$'\r': command not found" for a script whose lines end
# in CR, the EOL guard in the gate harness fails the script by name, and a
# byte-comparing gate sees "1,25c1,25" on identical text. core.autocrlf is a
# per-checkout setting, so the only place that survives a fresh clone is here.
#
# Scope is deliberately the ruled one -- native/{src,include,tools,cmake}, the
# root gate scripts and tools/ -- and NOT a global "* text=auto eol=lf": markdown
# keeps the bytes it was committed with, the evidence directories above stay
# -text, and this change carries no repository-wide renormalise. All 502 tracked
# files under these paths are already LF in both the index and the worktree
# (git ls-files --eol: 502 x "i/lf w/lf", zero CRLF, zero binaries), so pinning
# them rewrites nothing; it only stops a later checkout from handing them out
# with CR. The patterns are directory-scoped on purpose: native/third_party/**
# holds a tracked WebView2Loader.dll and stays unspecified (no text/eol attribute),
# so binary payloads keep their bytes. A future binary inside one of the pinned
# directories needs its own -text exception -- text=lf on a DLL would corrupt it.
/*.sh text eol=lf
/native/src/** text eol=lf
/native/include/** text eol=lf
/native/tools/** text eol=lf
/native/cmake/** text eol=lf
/tools/** text eol=lf
